# A pipe at the end of a statement: DS0103. Removing it may not be what was meant, so the fix is not machine-applicable.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | take 5 |;
'customers.csv' | count
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..49
  PIPELINE@0..23
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    TAKE_OP@15..21
      IDENT@15..19 "take"
      WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
      LITERAL@20..21
        LONG@20..21 "5"
    WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
    PIPE@22..23 "|"
  SEMICOLON@23..24 ";"
  WHITESPACE@24..25 "\n"
  PIPELINE@25..48
    LITERAL@25..40
      STRING@25..40 "'customers.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
    PIPE@41..42 "|"
    WHITESPACE@42..43 " "
    COUNT_OP@43..48
      IDENT@43..48 "count"
  WHITESPACE@48..49 "\n"

error[DS0103]: `|` with no operator after it
  --> query:1:23
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | take 5 |;
  |                       ^ expected an operator after this `|`
  |
  = help: remove the `|`, or add an operator after it, such as `take 10`
